{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1488482-my-homebrew-kiths","id":1488482,"title":"My Homebrew Kiths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-30T12:50:57-07:00","id":1488482,"title":"My Homebrew Kiths","content":"True Knight<br /> \u201cWe shall now seek that which we shall not find.\u201d-Sir Ector or Sir Lancelot (Le Morte de Arthur)<br /> A knight who was forced to live up to impossible standards of honor. Even after escaping from Arcadia they are still drawn to knightly behavior. However, their durance can also lead to cruelty as the changeling perceives any slight as an insult upon their honor or become jaded due to the dishonorable actions their keepers forced them to take and punished them for it. Some may even reject honor entirely in favor of thinking of themselves as better than everyone else. Still, many persist and keep their chivalry in mind. After all, sometimes absolute honor is like a world free of crime: impossible to attain but something you pursue anyway.<br /> Skill:<br /> When facing an opponent of lower clarity than them to protect someone or capture them alive, the True knight needs only three successes to achieve an exceptional success for weaponry.<br /> Blessing of the Lance:<br /> The True Knight can spend a point of glamour and roll dexterity+drive to be able to use all combat skills while driving a vehicle without any penalties related to both actions being done at once.<br /> <br /> Witch<br /> \u201cBubble, boil, toil, and trouble, fire burn and cauldron bubble.\u201d-The Three Witches (Macbeth)<br /> You were a master of magic, someone changed to curse others and preserve goblin fruit in your cauldron.<br /> Skill: <br /> When using occult to seek knowledge for the purpose of harming another being, you need only three successes to achieve an exceptional success.<br /> Witch\u2019s Cauldron:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll intelligence+crafts to create a potion out of a goblin fruit in any cooking implement that can hold water. These potions have the effects of the goblin fruit and you can have up to half your wyrd (rounded up) of them. The difference between these and goblin fruit is that you can give someone else a potion and have it count against your wyrd, not theirs.<br /> <br /> Assassin<br /> In Arcadia you were your keeper\u2019s hidden blade, a tool for swift and silent murder.<br /> Skill:<br /> When hiding from someone with the intention to kill them, the Assassin needs only three successes to achieve an exceptional success for stealth.<br /> Cloak of Shadows, Blade of Sorrow:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll strength+stealth to switch your stealth and either weaponry or firearms skills. Any bonuses you would normally gain for stealth is given to the weapon skill.<br /> <br /> Wizard<br /> \u201cDo not take me for some conjuror of cheap tricks!\u201d-Gandalf (LOTR)<br /> They say knowledge is power and magic comes from knowledge. Few personify this more than the wizards. They were the keepers of ancient and powerful secrets and the first on the lines to use those secrets for the benefit of the true fey.<br /> Skill:<br /> When convincing someone with persuade to give up knowledge related to magic, gain an exceptional success on three dice rather than five.<br /> Storm of Magic:<br /> Wizards personify the might of magic and can spend a point of glamour to cloak themselves in its power. Their voice booms and thunder can be heard when they speak. They gain a bonus equal to their wyrd, maximum of five, to intimidation rolls of either direct threats or interrogation.<br /> <br /> Blood-Axe<br /> Sometimes brutality is the best thing for warfare. That\u2019s what you are, a being used to brutally slaughter enemies on the battlefield or maybe an executioner, grim and terrible to behold. Either way, your enemies know to fear you.<br /> Skill:<br /> When brandishing a two-handed melee weapon, you only need three successes to achieve an exceptional success for intimidation.<br /> Bloodbath of War:<br /> Make a manipulation+weaponry or firearms roll and spend a point of glamour to absorb your enemy\u2019s blood into your weapon after inflicting damage. Take half of the damage and use each point to either heal 2B/1L damage or as a bonus to weapon damage for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Black Knight<br /> \u201cYou yellow-bellied bastards! I\u2019ll bite your legs off!\u201d-The Black Knight (Monty Python and the Holy Grail)<br /> Black Knights are put in places to guard them from passage. Bridges, gates, hallways, anything that can be guarded will be guarded.<br /> Skill:<br /> When fighting to stop someone from going through a passage, you only need three successes for an exceptional success with weaponry.<br /> Just a Flesh Wound:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll stamina+medicine to ignore all wound penalties and all conditions that result from a limb being targeted for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Djinn<br /> Trapped in a bottle, forced to be a light. Taken out only to serve your master. That was your life and your escape left you burned and scarred.<br /> Skill:<br /> Your heart is a fire, even if your body isn\u2019t. When making a persuasion roll to inspire anger, gain an exceptional success with three successes rather than five.<br /> Genie in the Lamp:<br /> Spend a glamour to force yourself into an object a maximum of two sizes smaller than you. When inside you are completely undetectable and can perceive the outside world; however, you cannot interact with it. If someone deliberately rubs the object, doesn\u2019t just brush it accidentally, you are forced out. Otherwise you can exit at the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> Schemer<br /> \u201cI did warn you not to trust me, you know.\u201d-Petyr Baelish (ASOIAF)<br /> Arcadia is a land of nobility. Great kingdoms and powerful houses and kings. And where there are powerful individuals, there are those seeking to undermine them. You were there to do just that: serve your keeper by undermining other true fey. Perhaps you ended up getting too good at undermining and turned on your keeper for escape or your own power\u2026<br /> Skill:<br /> When rolling empathy to give someone false information, gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> Always Keep your Foes Confused:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll manipulation+persuasion vs. wits+supernatural tolerance to either prevent an event from being connected to you by a target or to ensure it is connected to you by a target. The roll must be contested again if someone tells the target the event is or is not connected to you. If the target succeeds the second time, they believe what they are told about you.<br /> <br /> Serpentine (Conan reference)<br /> The form of a serpent is not necessarily connected with beasts. Its glimmering scales can indicate a fairest or its great coils can remind one of an ogre. Either way, serpents are beings connected to poison and death. This doesn\u2019t necessarily mean that serpentine beings are monsters, as it is often their keepers who used them in strange rituals, keep them in a dungeon to be forced to eat prisoner, or experiment on them to attain dark magic before chaining them up in a tower and forgetting about them.<br /> Skill:<br /> When making medicine rolls to create or cure poisons, gain an exceptional success on three successes rather than five.<br /> Serpent\u2019s Sight:<br /> By spending a point of glamour and rolling wits+stealth, the player is able to see the heat present in bodies and objects. This negates vision penalties. Additionally, the changeling can bite someone and gain a bonus to tracking them equal to half their wyrd rounded down, minimum of one.<br /> <br /> Grey<br /> Somewhere someone is being abducted by a flying saucer. In that same place, one of the others has gained a new test subject. But every scientist needs assistants and that\u2019s where greys come in.<br /> Skill:<br /> When making medicine rolls to practice surgery that involves permanently removing body parts, get an exceptional success with three successes rather than five.<br /> Beckoning Light:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll presence+empathy vs. composure+supernatural tolerance. If the grey wins, the target gains the insensate condition and walks towards the grey every turn until the condition ends.<br /> <br /> Storm Walker<br /> Maybe you were the wind, maybe a sorcerer that called the wind, or maybe you were a great bird whose wing-flaps were thunder. Whatever you were, your arrival signaled destruction as great winds rendered buildings asunder.<br /> Skill:<br /> When rolling to destroy large objects, gain an exceptional success on three successes instead of five.<br /> Wind Walker:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll dexterity+athletics to allow winds to carry you. You move at whatever speed the wind does and can allow yourself to be carried upwards by it. You must follow the wind but you take no damage if it slams you into an object or if you fall. The effect ends with the scene, the end of the wind, being stopped by an object, or when your character cancels it.<br /> <br /> Swamp Dweller<br /> \u201cWhat are you doing in my swamp?\u201d-Shrek (Shrek)<br /> Swamps are often dark and mysterious places full of diseases, parasites, and sinkholes. However, life still thrives there. Swamp Dwellers are changelings who were forced to survive deep within wetlands with all the horrors of Arcadia there.<br /> Skill:<br /> For the purpose of using athletics to jump through swamps or terrain that is commonly found in swamps, you only need three successes to achieve an exceptional success.<br /> Lurker of the Murky Water:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll Stamina+Survival to blend in with water. Maybe your skin changes color to match the mud, maybe you look a bit like a log, or maybe you just become easy to overlook. Whatever it is, it gives you a bonus to stealth equal to half your wyrd, rounded down with a minimum of one, as long as you stay in the water. In addition, you do not take penalties to perception rolls or vision from any murkiness within or plants covering the water.<br /> <br /> Wilderness Stalker<br /> Arcadia is home to vast landscapes and deep woods. Often scouts, spies, and dangerous game are needed for these areas. You were one of these things, specializing in hiding but capable of great violence when it comes down to it. A big cat lying in wait, an ogre who blends in with the wilderness, even a sentient thorn bush.<br /> Skill:<br /> Pick an environment that you lived in: woods, areas covered in deep snow, deep water, etc. You only need three successes to achieve an exceptional success on stealth rolls to hide in that environment.<br /> Wrath of the Cornered Beast:<br /> Spend a point of glamour to gain a burst of power. You do lethal damage with your unarmed attacks and gain two bonus dice on all attack rolls for the turn where you spend the glamour.<br /> <br /> Winged Legionnaire<br /> Great sky kingdoms rest on the clouds and floating islands of Arcadia. In these lands, war is fought on wings. While not traditional legionnaires, these changelings are nevertheless more than capable of fighting in the sky.<br /> Skill:<br /> When using ranged weaponry (guns or bows, not throwing weapons) from an elevated position, you only need three rolls for an exceptional success rather than five.<br /> Wings of Terror:<br /> Spend a point of glamour and roll dexterity+athletics to fly at twice your speed for the rest of the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}